<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Jerami Grant Paid $34.21m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Grant is paid <strong>$34.21m</strong> because a forward who scores and defends across positions is the most expensive thing in the league outside a star, and he has been paid at that level since 2020.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went 39th in 2014, so his first three seasons paid him <strong>$4.23m</strong> in total.</li>
<li><a href="/teams/detroit-pistons/">Detroit</a> gave him <strong>$60.01m</strong> in a sign-and-trade in 2020, which trebled his pay.</li>
<li>Portland then gave him <strong>$160m</strong> over five years in 2023.</li>
<li>He has been paid by six clubs and traded three times inside contracts.</li>
<li>The last season is a player option, so nothing past 2026-27 is settled.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has earned <strong>$205.83m</strong> in career salary after being taken 39th.</p>

</div><div class="bde-shortcode-506-159 bde-shortcode"><div class="nba-fin" data-nba-fin="why">
